<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n44965" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐροέω</span></b> , (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὔροος</span>)
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>flow well</i> or
				<i>abundantly</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>CP</u>
				5.6.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> metaph.,
				<i>go on well, be favourable</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅταν δ᾽ ὁ δαίμων εὐροῇ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					601
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῶν πραγμάτων αὐτῷ εὐροούντων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plb.
					4.48.11
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τῆς τύχης εὐροούσης</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					2.45
				</span></i>
			; of men, <i>to be prosperous</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arr.
				<u>Epict.</u>
				1.1.22
			</span></i>,<i><span class="en">
				3.10.10
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>to be fluent, speak successfully</i>, <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Alex.</u>
				53
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
